{
  "_doc": "How each sub-vertical NAMES the things the v7.0 catalogue asks about, so a collector translates a cell's question into the entity's own words before it searches (2026-10-09: an insurance broker's P2C2 queries carried banking vocabulary — 'thin-file', 'pre-qualification without full application' — and found unrelated companies). `customer`, `product`, `application` and `account` replace the catalogue's generic nouns; `artefacts` are the public things that would show a capability; `systems` are the platform names that betray one; `not_applicable` names catalogue vocabulary that does not exist in this business — a cell asking about it is searched as its nearest equivalent, and the absence says which.",
  "CU": {"customer": "member", "product": "share/loan product", "application": "membership or loan application", "account": "share account",
         "artefacts": ["online banking", "mobile app", "member portal", "annual report", "NCUA call report", "board minutes"],
         "systems": ["Symitar", "Corelation KeyStone", "Alkami", "Q2", "MeridianLink", "Jack Henry"],
         "not_applicable": []},
